        {
            "id": "0.3300477061931668",
            "type": "note-node",
            "position": {
                "x": 210.69196337342333,
                "y": -21.456620208490804
            },
            "origin": [
                0,
                0
            ],
            "data": {
                "label": "SDR Types",
                "sequence": "0",
                "user_properties": [
                    [
                        "rdfs:comment",
                        "We define two types of SDRs: devices and computers.\n\n\nSDR computers are considered to be self-contained radio\nsystems that have onboard compute capability (e.g., DSP, FPGA).\nExample: Flexradio Flex-8400M\n\n\nSDR devices are those without onboard computer and \ntherfeore require a host computer for running the actual waveform. \nExample: RTL-SDR\n\n\nOn a spacecraft/satellite, you'd expect to see an SDR computer."
                    ]
                ]
            },
            "measured": {
                "width": 368,
                "height": 251
            },
            "selected": false,
            "dragging": false
        },
        {
